    <edx>
      <text>
        For AMD CPUs, bits[0:9] are a replica of leaf 1's EDX[0:9] bits.  Similarly,
        bits[12:17] are a replica of leaf1's EDX[12:17] bits.  Same for bit 24.

        For Transmeta CPUs, it's not an exact replica: feature bit11 (SEP) and
        feature bit18 (PSN) are only reported at leaf1's EDX, while FCMOV feature
        bit16 is only reported here at this extended leaf's EDX.

        In case of redundancy, Linux just uses the Intel-compatible bits by default.
      </text>
